  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative focused on data analytics, AI algorithms, and cloud storage optimization. It was introduced in June/July 2023 with a kickoff led by Sarah Tan (Analytics) and later Marcus Cole, with a Phase One budget of $500,000. Key developments include initial findings suggesting a 20% efficiency increase via AI, a strategic partnership with TechInnovate, and team expansions adding experts in machine learning and cloud computing. The project has progressed through design and idea-gathering phases, with a focus on predictive analytics and data visualization. Phase Two highlights a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with updates shared in meetings in August and November. Training budgets of $15,000 have been approved for coding and management teams, and development is led by Omar Jensen."
